# Special events: conferences and other services the church hosts.
# ------------------------------------
# One row per session. A recording named with the session's date and code,
# e.g. 110726RC2.mp3, is processed like a sermon, using the speaker, title
# and passage from its row. A code is only recognized on the dates listed
# here, so add the rows before the event (or at least before processing).
#
# FORMAT:
#   date,code,speaker,title,scripture,event
#   - date: 11/6/26 (or 110626)
#   - code: two letters plus a session number when there's more than one
#     that day: RC1, RC2 (Reformation Conference), MC1 (Missions Conference)...
#     AM, PM, HE and SS are taken by Sunday services.
#   - speaker: full name with title, as it should appear in the documents
#   - title and scripture: optional; leave blank if not known yet
#   - event: the name shown in the documents, e.g. Reformation Conference
#   - Put quotes around a value that contains a comma.
#   - Lines starting with # are comments and are ignored.
#
# Example (a Friday evening session and two Saturday morning sessions):
#   11/6/26,RC1,Dr. First Speaker,Title of the Friday Session,2 Timothy 3:14-17,Reformation Conference
#   11/7/26,RC1,Dr. Second Speaker,"Title, With a Comma",Revelation 21:1-4,Reformation Conference
#   11/7/26,RC2,Dr. First Speaker,Title of the Third Session,,Reformation Conference
#
date,code,speaker,title,scripture,event
